{"changes":["eka-cli/vendored.yaml (new): records standardRelease (the eka-standard release the bytes came from) and the sha256 of each vendored artifact — EKA, templates/hooks/pre-commit, templates/hooks/pre-push.","eka-cli/standardembed_pin_test.go (new): TestVendoredStandardMatchesPin recomputes each digest from the real file in the tree and names the expected eka-standard release on failure; TestVendoredPinCoversEmbeddedArtifacts fails when an embedded artifact has no pin, so a newly vendored file cannot bypass the check.","eka-cli/scripts/pin-vendored (new, go run ./scripts/pin-vendored): reports drift by default and rewrites the digests with -write, exiting non-zero on drift in report mode. Refreshing a copy from eka-standard and re-pinning it is now one operation instead of a manual edit that invites the drift the pin exists to catch."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Pinned the vendored eka-standard artifacts with recorded sha256 digests and a refresh script, so drift from the standard release is detectable.","tests":["go test . -run TestVendored -\u003e PASS (both tests).","go run ./scripts/pin-vendored -\u003e all three artifacts report ok, exit 0.","Non-vacuous proof: appended a trailing line to EKA and reran — the pin test failed with 'vendored artifact EKA does not match eka-standard release 1.3: sha256 = f34fb..., expected fc66c...' plus the refresh instruction, and the script exited non-zero. EKA restored and the digest re-verified as fc66c9eb...","go build ./... , go vet ./... , gofmt -l . -\u003e clean."]}